1240:main.c        ****                 /*
1241:main.c        ****                  * P-control (KP) keeps the two wheels' encoder counts
1242:main.c        ****                  * in sync so the robot drives straight: master motor
1243:main.c        ****                  * runs at a fixed MASTER_PWM, slave motor's PWM is
1244:main.c        ****                  * nudged up/down by KP * error.
1245:main.c        ****                  *
1246:main.c        ****                  * Forward motion drives relative_c2 (and relative_c1)
1247:main.c        ****                  * DOWN toward a negative target, so "ahead" means
1248:main.c        ****                  * "more negative". error = slave - master: if slave
1249:main.c        ****                  * has gone more negative than master (slave ahead),
1250:main.c        ****                  * error < 0 -> slave PWM decreases (slow down); if
1251:main.c        ****                  * slave lags (less negative than master), error > 0
1252:main.c        ****                  * -> slave PWM increases (speed up). Negative feedback.
1253:main.c        ****                  */
